diagonal and G\"odel's incompleteness sentence are the same Inclosure construction at successive overflow levels; the
grammar occupies Level~2, co-typed with the Millennium Problems. This document is the $\delta$ half of a Frobenius pair
with its companion (\emph{So Below}); $\mu \circ \delta = \text{id}$: the grammar applied to its own derivation returns
itself. All eight open questions from the original manuscript are resolved in \S VIII.
