756	\subsubsection{Algebraic Operations}
757	Algebraic operations add new structure to $\mathcal{C}$ by equipping it with a tensor product,
758	\textbf{A1 --- Monoidal structure}: Equip $\mathcal{C}$ with $\otimes: \mathcal{C} \times
759	\mathcal{C} \to \mathcal{C}$
760	and unit $I$. This introduces the arity primitive: $n$-ary operations are maps $A^{\otimes n} \to B$. The arity of the
761	generators of $\mathcal{C}$ under $\otimes$ determines $S$ (stoichiometry). Symmetry of $\otimes$
762	(braiding isomorphism
763	$\sigma_{AB}: A \otimes B \cong B \otimes A$) determines $P$.
764	\textbf{A2 --- Monad}: A monad $(T, \eta: \text{Id} \to T, \mu: T^2 \to T)$ on $\mathcal{C}$ packages an algebraic
765	theory. The spectral properties of the natural transformation $\mu$ determine $\text{{\igprimfont ⊤}}$: if the unit
766	$\eta$ and multiplication $\mu$ produce dynamics that rapidly equilibrate, the system is
767	\text{{\igfont 𐑘}}; if they
768	produce a gapped ground state (a terminal coalgebra), it is \text{{\igfont 𐑪}}; intermediate cases
769	give \text{{\igfont 𐑤}} and \text{{\igfont 𐑧}}.
770	\textbf{A3 --- Dagger-compact structure}: Adding duals $A^*$ with $\eta_A: I \to A^* \otimes A$ and
771	$\varepsilon_A: A
772	\otimes A^* \to I$ satisfying the snake equations gives dagger-compact structure. This controls fidelity: non-unital
773	$\varepsilon$ corresponds to \text{{\igfont 𐑱}} (information loss); unital gives \text{{\igfont 𐑞}}; fully coherent
774	(quantum) composition gives \text{{\igfont 𐑐}}.
775	\textbf{A4 --- Enrichment}: Enriching $\mathcal{C}$ over a monoidal category $\mathcal{V}$ --- replacing hom-sets with
776	hom-objects in $\mathcal{V}$ --- determines the interaction grammar. Enrichment over $\mathbf{Set}$
777	\text{{\igfont 𐑠}} (morphisms compose sequentially). Enrichment over $\mathbf{Set}^\times$ (product
778	\text{{\igfont 𐑝}}. Enrichment over $\mathbf{Set}^+$ (coproduct/choice) gives \text{{\igfont 𐑜}}. Enrichment over a
779	broadcast monoid (one-to-many maps) gives \text{{\igfont 𐑵}}.
780	\textbf{A5 --- G\"odel arithmetization} (requires A2): Given a monad $(T, \eta, \mu)$ on
781	$\mathcal{C}$, assign an
782	injective effective coding $\mathbf{g}: \text{Mor}(\mathcal{C}) \to \mathbb{N}$ such that:
783	
784	\begin{itemize}
785	 \item \emph{Injectivity}: distinct morphisms receive distinct codes ($\mathbf{g}$ is 1-to-1)
786	 \item \emph{Effectiveness}: the code of a composition $\mathbf{g}(f \circ h)$ is primitive-recursive in
787	$\mathbf{g}(f)$ and $\mathbf{g}(h)$
788	 \item \emph{Self-applicability}: the monad $T$ (from A2) acts on codes, so $T(\mathbf{g}(f))$ is a morphism code in
789	$\mathcal{C}$
790	\end{itemize}
791	
792	This is the \textbf{arithmetic Yoneda}: where I4 embeds $\mathcal{C}$ into $\hat{\mathcal{C}}$ preserving all
793	structure, A5 embeds $\mathcal{C}$ into $\mathbb{N}$ preserving only the primitive-recursive structure. A5 does not
794	generate a new primitive. It is the bridge between Stage 3 and Stage 4: it installs the internal self-awareness that
795	makes L4 and L6 non-trivial when asked of the enriched $\mathcal{C}$.
796	\textbf{Why exactly five algebraic operations?} The five operations correspond to the five independent enrichment
797	layers of a category recognized by enriched category theory. A1 (monoidal product) adds a binary
798	A2 (monad) adds an endofunctor with algebraic theory. A3 (dagger-compact structure) adds duals. A4
799	(enrichment) changes
800	the fundamental nature of morphism sets. A5 (arithmetic coding) adds self-awareness. No sixth enrichment exists that is
801	not a composite of these five: for instance, a traced monoidal structure is a special case of A1+A3; a closed monoidal
802	structure is A1+A4; a star-autonomous structure is A1+A3+A4. The five are algebraically independent: one can have a
803	monoidal category without a monad (A1 without A2), a dagger category without a monoidal product (A3 without A1), and so
804	on. Any category can be enriched (A4) over any monoidal category, independently of A1--A3. The arithmetic coding (A5)
805	is independent of all except A2 (it requires a monad to make sense of `\texttt{code} of a morphism"). The five are thus the
806	basis of the enrichment lattice, not an arbitrary enumeration.
